# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nested tag-scope + try/finally cleanup ordering per row 7 §6.3;
#         verifies that the unwind walker pops TAG_SCOPE entries in innermost-
#         first order through nested scopes, executing each onleave body before
#         continuing outward.
#
# blocked: `onleave` keyword not yet supported on tag-scope — parse error (deferred-v1.x)
#   (T39 chk-driver reason stale; the chk driver uses urbi -i / urbi_repl_eval
#   which has always handled fork separators; the real blocker is `onleave`)
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.5 probe):
#   This fixture uses the TAG_SCOPE onleave syntax (`tag: { body } onleave handler`)
#   which is v1.x deferred (PARSE-033 closure; tag_prefix.onleave is always NULL
#   at v1.0).  The AT_WATCHER form (`at (cond) body onleave handler`) IS
#   supported and is tested in tests/chk/reactive/at/at_onleave.chk and
#   tests/chk/reactive/at/onleave_cascade.chk.  This fixture must wait for
#   tag-scope onleave parse/emit support.  Probing yields:
#     "expected '}'" on the `onleave` lines (confirmed v0.13.5).
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: log records cleanup in innermost-first order "ioIO".
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5):
#   var log = "";
#   var outer = Tag.new;
#   var inner = Tag.new;
#   try {
#     outer: {
#       try {
#         inner: { outer.stop() }
#           onleave { log = log + "i" }
#       } finally { log = log + "I" }
#     } onleave { log = log + "o" }
#   } finally { log = log + "O" };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "ioIO"
